   "source": [
    "<h4>What are data structures ?<h4> \n",
    "ans: Data Structures is the way to store complex data /sh"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "65f50981",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "types of data structures"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "558e6e7a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Primitive data structure : int float char bool etc <br>\n",
    "Abstract data structure : list stack linked list etc"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "9cc42c5d",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "raw"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "// int\n",
    "void fun(int x)\n",
    "\n",
    "// string\n",
    "void fun(string s)\n",
    "\n",
    "// array\n",
    "void fun(int arr[], int size)\n",
    "\n",
    "// vector - read only\n",
    "void fun(const vector<int>& v)\n",
    "\n",
    "// vector - modify\n",
    "void fun(vector<int>& v)\n",
    "\n",
    "// 2D vector\n",
    "void fun(vector<vector<int>>& v)\n",
    "\n",
    "& → work with the original object instead of making a copy.\n",
    "const & → work with the original but don't modify it."
   ]
  }
